    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:</i>&nbsp;<i><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide\">Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide</a></i> </p><p><b>Manufactured By:</b> The <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Gand\" title=\"Gand\">Gand</a> (<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Species\" title=\"Species\">Species</a>) </p><p><b>Applicable To:</b> Any Weapon with a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Stun\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Stun\">Stun</a> Setting </p><p>The <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Gand\" title=\"Gand\">Gand</a> Species, peculiar and often incomprehensible, specializes in crafting Weapons that immobilizes opponents. </p><p><b>Weapons:</b> If a Gand Manufacture Weapon moves a target down the Condition Track with it's <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Stun\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Stun\">Stun</a> damage, that target has its speed halved until it returns to its normal state (all conditions removed); a target that is -4 steps down the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Condition_Track\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Condition Track\">Condition Track</a> (at the -10 step) is <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Immobilized\" title=\"Immobilized\">Immobilized</a> instead. Gand Manufacture Weapons are difficult to operate, and all Gand Manufacture Weapons are considered <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Exotic_Weapons\" title=\"Exotic Weapons\">Exotic Weapons</a> for purposes of proficiency (except to a member of the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Gand\" title=\"Gand\">Gand</a> Species). </p>",
